<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hardened-runtime entitlements for the Developer ID build (M4-05).

  Deliberately almost empty. What is *not* here matters more than what is:

  * `com.apple.security.app-sandbox` is false, and stated explicitly rather than
    omitted. Spec §3 ships outside the App Store precisely so the app can read
    and write an arbitrary user-chosen notes folder with plain POSIX calls and
    hand those paths to Finder; a sandbox would force security-scoped bookmarks
    on every note. This also means Sparkle needs no XPC services and no
    `SUEnableInstallerLauncherService` / `SUEnableDownloaderService` Info.plist
    keys — `Tools/make_app.sh` strips `Sparkle.framework/Versions/B/XPCServices`
    for exactly that reason (ADR-045).

  * No `com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory` and no
    `com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit`. Checked against what the app actually
    does: `FilawayCore/Embeddings` calls `MLModel.compileModel(at:)` at first
    launch and then `MLModel(contentsOf:)` with `MLComputeUnits.all`. Core ML
    compilation runs out of process in the system's own compiler service and the
    compiled `.mlmodelc` it loads back is data, not code, so neither the JIT nor
    the unsigned-memory exception applies. Add one only if a notarized build is
    observed to crash in Espresso/ANE — never speculatively, since both widen
    the attack surface a hardened runtime exists to narrow.

  * No `com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation`. Every bundled
    executable — the app, Sparkle.framework, Autoupdate, Updater.app — is signed
    by the same Developer ID in one inner-out pass, so library validation is
    satisfied without being disabled.

  * No Keychain access group. Outside the sandbox, `AIConnectionManager`'s
    Keychain items are reachable without an entitlement; adding a group would
    only make the items harder to migrate later.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
    <false/>
</dict>
</plist>
